::Q001::[markdown]aorist (1) active optative 1st sing. of the verb “I order”:{
	~%-100%ἐλύσαμεν#Incorrect. **ἐλύσαμεν** is the aorist (1) active indicative 1st pl. of the verb “I loosen” (Ch. 2).
	~%50%κελεύσαιμι#Correct: **κελεύσαιμι** is the correct form for aorist (1) active optative 1st sing. of the verb “I order” (Chapter 3).
	~%-100%παιδεύσαις#Incorrect. **παιδεύσαις** is the aorist (1) active optative 2nd sing. of the verb “I educate” (Ch. 3).
	~%50%-#Correct: **-** is the correct form for aorist (1) active optative 1st sing. of the verb “I order” (Chapter 3).
	~%-100%ἐπέμψατε#Incorrect. **ἐπέμψατε** is the aorist (1) active indicative 2nd pl. of the verb “I send” (Ch. 3).
}


::Q002::[markdown]κελεύοιμεν:{
	~%-100%aorist (1) active indicative 1st pl. of the verb “I order”#Incorrect. The aorist (1) active indicative 1st pl. of the verb “I order” is **ἐκελεύσαμεν** (Ch. 2).
	~%-100%present active indicative 2nd sing. of the verb “I educate”#Incorrect. The present active indicative 2nd sing. of the verb “I educate” is **παιδεύεις** (Ch. 2).
	~%-100%pluperfect active indicative 1st pl. of the verb “I educate”#Incorrect. The pluperfect active indicative 1st pl. of the verb “I educate” is **ἐπεπαιδεύκεμεν** (Ch. 3).
	~%-100%aorist (1) active subjunctive 1st sing. of the verb “I educate”#Incorrect. The aorist (1) active subjunctive 1st sing. of the verb “I educate” is **παιδεύσω** (Ch. 3).
	~%100%present active optative 1st pl. of the verb “I order”#Correct: **κελεύοιμεν** is present active optative 1st pl. of the verb “I order” (Chapter 3).
}


